window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b346-f204fd978b254920.json"]={sha256:"f204fd978b254920a5b0e3837c983e203e6d03be2073847c7ef1ebfeebb14626",value:{"id":"b346","title":"浮動式道床減振","titleEn":"Floating-slab track vibration isolation","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"浮動式道床減振以「浮動道床隔振共振及附加質量效應」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。浮動式道床利用彈性支承把軌道質量與基礎分開，低頻共振與高頻隔振同時存在；隔振效果必須指定輸入位置、輸出位置與頻率範圍。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops floating-slab isolation resonance and added-mass effects through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. Floating slabs separate track mass from the foundation through resilient supports, creating both low-frequency resonance and high-frequency isolation; performance needs specified input and output positions and frequency range. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-track","subcategoryTitle":"軌道與土建工程","subcategoryTitleEn":"Track and civil engineering","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-track","learningTags":["rail","rail-track","track"],"architectureFamily":"rail-track","architectureNodes":[["輪軌激振","Wheel-rail excitation"],["浮置板質量","Floating mass"],["隔振支承","Isolation support"],["基礎反應","Foundation response"],["位移行程","Displacement travel"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-track","labels":["輪軌激振","浮置板質量","隔振支承","基礎反應","位移行程"],"labelsEn":["Wheel-rail excitation","Floating mass","Isolation support","Foundation response","Displacement travel"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg；y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)=3.1831 Hz。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=3.33846 Hz。模型邊界：線性單自由度且基礎固定；計算無阻尼固有頻率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, k=4000000 N/m；y=m*g/k*1000=24.525 mm。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=26.9775 mm。模型邊界：重力載荷平均且支承線性；不含動載與限位接觸；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg; y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)=3.1831 Hz. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.33846 Hz. Boundary: Linear single-degree system with a fixed base; the calculated frequency is undamped; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, k=4000000 N/m; y=m*g/k*1000=24.525 mm. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=26.9775 mm. Boundary: Gravity load is steady and support linear; dynamic load and travel-stop contact are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b346-v16-s1","title":"隔振固有頻率與靜載壓縮量","titleEn":"Isolation natural frequency & Static support compression","description":"本階段聚焦「隔振固有頻率」與「靜載壓縮量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Isolation natural frequency\" and \"Static support compression\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b346-v16-01","title":"隔振固有頻率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Isolation natural frequency: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「隔振固有頻率」如何影響浮動式道床減振的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Isolation natural frequency” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floating-slab track vibration isolation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"固有頻率由剛度質量比的平方根決定。本模型把 k 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 3.33846 Hz。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。線性單自由度且基礎固定；計算無阻尼固有頻率。使用自由衰減頻率作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；支承硬化會提高固有頻率，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「隔振固有頻率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Natural frequency follows the square root of stiffness-to-mass ratio. In this model, k is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 3.33846 Hz. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Linear single-degree system with a fixed base; the calculated frequency is undamped. Use free-decay frequency as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Support hardening raises natural frequency; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Isolation natural frequency” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg；y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)=3.1831 Hz。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg; y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)=3.1831 Hz.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承硬化會提高固有頻率」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support hardening raises natural frequency.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「隔振固有頻率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Isolation natural frequency”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-01-k1","title":"隔振固有頻率","titleEn":"Isolation natural frequency","text":"固有頻率由剛度質量比的平方根決定。本模型把 k 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 3.33846 Hz。","textEn":"Natural frequency follows the square root of stiffness-to-mass ratio. In this model, k is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承硬化會提高固有頻率 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support hardening raises natural frequency. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「隔振固有頻率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Isolation natural frequency\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承硬化會提高固有頻率","固有頻率由剛度質量比的平方根決定。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承到底會使線性隔振失效"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support hardening raises natural frequency.","Natural frequency follows the square root of stiffness-to-mass ratio.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"固有頻率由剛度質量比的平方根決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Natural frequency follows the square root of stiffness-to-mass ratio. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b346-v16-02","title":"隔振固有頻率：定量估算","titleEn":"Isolation natural frequency: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隔振固有頻率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Isolation natural frequency” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg；y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)=3.1831 Hz。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=3.33846 Hz。模型邊界：線性單自由度且基礎固定；計算無阻尼固有頻率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg; y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)=3.1831 Hz. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.33846 Hz. Boundary: Linear single-degree system with a fixed base; the calculated frequency is undamped; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以自由衰減頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型質量、靜剛度與經阻尼修正的自由衰減頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use free-decay frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg；y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)=3.1831 Hz。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=3.33846 Hz。模型邊界：線性單自由度且基礎固定；計算無阻尼固有頻率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg; y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)=3.1831 Hz. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.33846 Hz. Boundary: Linear single-degree system with a fixed base; the calculated frequency is undamped; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「隔振固有頻率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Isolation natural frequency\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重心偏移使單支承過載","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg；y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)=3.1831 Hz。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg; y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)=3.1831 Hz."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg；y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)=3.1831 Hz。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg; y=sqrt(k/m)/(2*pi)=3.1831 Hz. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b346-v16-03","title":"隔振固有頻率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Isolation natural frequency: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隔振固有頻率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Isolation natural frequency” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以自由衰減頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型質量、靜剛度與經阻尼修正的自由衰減頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「隔振固有頻率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use free-decay frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model mass, static stiffness and damping-corrected free-decay frequency, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Isolation natural frequency. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「隔振固有頻率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出線性單自由度且基礎固定；計算無阻尼固有頻率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由支承硬化會提高固有頻率造成偏離的合成觀察，以自由衰減頻率說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Isolation natural frequency, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Linear single-degree system with a fixed base; the calculated frequency is undamped. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Support hardening raises natural frequency. Explain which evidence in free-decay frequency distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：支承硬化會提高固有頻率。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Support hardening raises natural frequency. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以自由衰減頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型質量、靜剛度與經阻尼修正的自由衰減頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「隔振固有頻率」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use free-decay frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model mass, static stiffness and damping-corrected free-decay frequency, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Isolation natural frequency. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「隔振固有頻率」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出線性單自由度且基礎固定；計算無阻尼固有頻率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由支承硬化會提高固有頻率造成偏離的合成觀察，以自由衰減頻率說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Isolation natural frequency, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Linear single-degree system with a fixed base; the calculated frequency is undamped. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Support hardening raises natural frequency. Explain which evidence in free-decay frequency distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「隔振固有頻率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Isolation natural frequency\"?","options":["本單元以自由衰減頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型質量、靜剛度與經阻尼修正的自由衰減頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：異物橋接會旁路隔振支承"],"optionsEn":["Use free-decay frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以自由衰減頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型質量、靜剛度與經阻尼修正的自由衰減頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use free-decay frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b346-v16-04","title":"隔振固有頻率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Isolation natural frequency: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隔振固有頻率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Isolation natural frequency” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支承硬化會提高固有頻率。這個失效與「隔振固有頻率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查自由衰減頻率，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Support hardening raises natural frequency. This failure and a measurement bias in Isolation natural frequency can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check free-decay frequency rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用自由衰減頻率作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；支承硬化會提高固有頻率，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Support hardening raises natural frequency; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承硬化會提高固有頻率」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support hardening raises natural frequency.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支承硬化會提高固有頻率。這個失效與「隔振固有頻率」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查自由衰減頻率，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Support hardening raises natural frequency. This failure and a measurement bias in Isolation natural frequency can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check free-decay frequency rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「隔振固有頻率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Isolation natural frequency\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","支承硬化會提高固有頻率。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承到底會使線性隔振失效"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Support hardening raises natural frequency.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"支承硬化會提高固有頻率。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Support hardening raises natural frequency. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b346-v16-05","title":"靜載壓縮量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Static support compression: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「靜載壓縮量」如何影響浮動式道床減振的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Static support compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floating-slab track vibration isolation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"靜壓縮提供剛度量級檢查，但不能直接證明動態隔振。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 26.9775 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。重力載荷平均且支承線性；不含動載與限位接觸。使用靜態高度與總載重作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；支承到底會使線性隔振失效，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「靜載壓縮量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Static compression checks stiffness scale but does not establish dynamic isolation. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 26.9775 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Gravity load is steady and support linear; dynamic load and travel-stop contact are excluded. Use static height and total load as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Static support compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, k=4000000 N/m；y=m*g/k*1000=24.525 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, k=4000000 N/m; y=m*g/k*1000=24.525 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承到底會使線性隔振失效」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「靜載壓縮量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Static support compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-05-k1","title":"靜載壓縮量","titleEn":"Static support compression","text":"靜壓縮提供剛度量級檢查，但不能直接證明動態隔振。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 26.9775 mm。","textEn":"Static compression checks stiffness scale but does not establish dynamic isolation. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承到底會使線性隔振失效 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「靜載壓縮量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Static support compression\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承到底會使線性隔振失效","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示","靜壓縮提供剛度量級檢查，但不能直接證明動態隔振。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient.","Static compression checks stiffness scale but does not establish dynamic isolation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"靜壓縮提供剛度量級檢查，但不能直接證明動態隔振。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Static compression checks stiffness scale but does not establish dynamic isolation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b346-v16-06","title":"靜載壓縮量：定量估算","titleEn":"Static support compression: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「靜載壓縮量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Static support compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, k=4000000 N/m；y=m*g/k*1000=24.525 mm。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=26.9775 mm。模型邊界：重力載荷平均且支承線性；不含動載與限位接觸；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, k=4000000 N/m; y=m*g/k*1000=24.525 mm. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=26.9775 mm. Boundary: Gravity load is steady and support linear; dynamic load and travel-stop contact are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以靜態高度與總載重區分模型與觀察，先用模型總重、各支承高度及靜態載入卸載建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use static height and total load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, k=4000000 N/m；y=m*g/k*1000=24.525 mm。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=26.9775 mm。模型邊界：重力載荷平均且支承線性；不含動載與限位接觸；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, k=4000000 N/m; y=m*g/k*1000=24.525 mm. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=26.9775 mm. Boundary: Gravity load is steady and support linear; dynamic load and travel-stop contact are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「靜載壓縮量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Static support compression\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, k=4000000 N/m；y=m*g/k*1000=24.525 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, k=4000000 N/m; y=m*g/k*1000=24.525 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, k=4000000 N/m；y=m*g/k*1000=24.525 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, k=4000000 N/m; y=m*g/k*1000=24.525 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b346-v16-07","title":"靜載壓縮量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Static support compression: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「靜載壓縮量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Static support compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以靜態高度與總載重區分模型與觀察，先用模型總重、各支承高度及靜態載入卸載建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「靜載壓縮量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use static height and total load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model total weight, individual support heights and static loading-unloading, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Static support compression. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「靜載壓縮量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出重力載荷平均且支承線性；不含動載與限位接觸如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由支承到底會使線性隔振失效造成偏離的合成觀察，以靜態高度與總載重說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Static support compression, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Gravity load is steady and support linear; dynamic load and travel-stop contact are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation. Explain which evidence in static height and total load distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：支承到底會使線性隔振失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以靜態高度與總載重區分模型與觀察，先用模型總重、各支承高度及靜態載入卸載建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「靜載壓縮量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use static height and total load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model total weight, individual support heights and static loading-unloading, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Static support compression. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「靜載壓縮量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出重力載荷平均且支承線性；不含動載與限位接觸如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由支承到底會使線性隔振失效造成偏離的合成觀察，以靜態高度與總載重說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Static support compression, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Gravity load is steady and support linear; dynamic load and travel-stop contact are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation. Explain which evidence in static height and total load distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「靜載壓縮量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Static support compression\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以靜態高度與總載重區分模型與觀察，先用模型總重、各支承高度及靜態載入卸載建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use static height and total load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Standing water can create additional contact damping."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以靜態高度與總載重區分模型與觀察，先用模型總重、各支承高度及靜態載入卸載建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use static height and total load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b346-v16-08","title":"靜載壓縮量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Static support compression: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「靜載壓縮量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Static support compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支承到底會使線性隔振失效。這個失效與「靜載壓縮量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查靜態高度與總載重，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation. This failure and a measurement bias in Static support compression can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check static height and total load rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用靜態高度與總載重作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；支承到底會使線性隔振失效，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承到底會使線性隔振失效」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支承到底會使線性隔振失效。這個失效與「靜載壓縮量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查靜態高度與總載重，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation. This failure and a measurement bias in Static support compression can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check static height and total load rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「靜載壓縮量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Static support compression\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示","支承到底會使線性隔振失效。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient.","Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"支承到底會使線性隔振失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b346-v16-s2","title":"阻尼比估算與頻率比辨認","titleEn":"Damping ratio estimate & Frequency-ratio identification","description":"本階段聚焦「阻尼比估算」與「頻率比辨認」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Damping ratio estimate\" and \"Frequency-ratio identification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b346-v16-09","title":"阻尼比估算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Damping ratio estimate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「阻尼比估算」如何影響浮動式道床減振的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Damping ratio estimate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floating-slab track vibration isolation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"阻尼比將黏性阻尼相對於臨界阻尼正規化。本模型把 c 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.0825 1。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。黏性阻尼與線性剛度已知；不把庫侖摩擦視為固定黏性阻尼。使用衰減包絡與頻率作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「阻尼比估算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Damping ratio normalizes viscous damping by critical damping. In this model, c is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.0825 1. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Viscous damping and linear stiffness are known; Coulomb friction is not treated as constant viscous damping. Use decay envelope and frequency as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Damping ratio estimate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：c=30000 Ns/m, k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg；y=c/(2*sqrt(k*m))=0.075 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: c=30000 Ns/m, k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg; y=c/(2*sqrt(k*m))=0.075 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「阻尼比估算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Damping ratio estimate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-09-k1","title":"阻尼比估算","titleEn":"Damping ratio estimate","text":"阻尼比將黏性阻尼相對於臨界阻尼正規化。本模型把 c 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.0825 1。","textEn":"Damping ratio normalizes viscous damping by critical damping. In this model, c is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「阻尼比估算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Damping ratio estimate\" is correct?","options":["阻尼比將黏性阻尼相對於臨界阻尼正規化。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動"],"optionsEn":["Damping ratio normalizes viscous damping by critical damping.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"阻尼比將黏性阻尼相對於臨界阻尼正規化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Damping ratio normalizes viscous damping by critical damping. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b346-v16-10","title":"阻尼比估算：定量估算","titleEn":"Damping ratio estimate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「阻尼比估算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Damping ratio estimate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：c=30000 Ns/m, k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg；y=c/(2*sqrt(k*m))=0.075 1。只把 c 增加百分之十，y=0.0825 1。模型邊界：黏性阻尼與線性剛度已知；不把庫侖摩擦視為固定黏性阻尼；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: c=30000 Ns/m, k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg; y=c/(2*sqrt(k*m))=0.075 1. Increasing only c with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.0825 1. Boundary: Viscous damping and linear stiffness are known; Coulomb friction is not treated as constant viscous damping; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以衰減包絡與頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型自由衰減包絡、多振幅試驗及頻率估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use decay envelope and frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：c=30000 Ns/m, k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg；y=c/(2*sqrt(k*m))=0.075 1。只把 c 增加百分之十，y=0.0825 1。模型邊界：黏性阻尼與線性剛度已知；不把庫侖摩擦視為固定黏性阻尼；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: c=30000 Ns/m, k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg; y=c/(2*sqrt(k*m))=0.075 1. Increasing only c with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.0825 1. Boundary: Viscous damping and linear stiffness are known; Coulomb friction is not treated as constant viscous damping; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「阻尼比估算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Damping ratio estimate\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重心偏移使單支承過載","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：c=30000 Ns/m, k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：異物橋接會旁路隔振支承"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: c=30000 Ns/m, k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg; y=c/(2*sqrt(k*m))=0.075 1.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：c=30000 Ns/m, k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg；y=c/(2*sqrt(k*m))=0.075 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: c=30000 Ns/m, k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg; y=c/(2*sqrt(k*m))=0.075 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b346-v16-11","title":"阻尼比估算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Damping ratio estimate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「阻尼比估算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Damping ratio estimate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以衰減包絡與頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型自由衰減包絡、多振幅試驗及頻率估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「阻尼比估算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use decay envelope and frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model free-decay envelopes, several vibration amplitudes and frequency estimates, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Damping ratio estimate. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「阻尼比估算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出黏性阻尼與線性剛度已知；不把庫侖摩擦視為固定黏性阻尼如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示造成偏離的合成觀察，以衰減包絡與頻率說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Damping ratio estimate, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Viscous damping and linear stiffness are known; Coulomb friction is not treated as constant viscous damping. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient. Explain which evidence in decay envelope and frequency distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以衰減包絡與頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型自由衰減包絡、多振幅試驗及頻率估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「阻尼比估算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use decay envelope and frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model free-decay envelopes, several vibration amplitudes and frequency estimates, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Damping ratio estimate. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「阻尼比估算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出黏性阻尼與線性剛度已知；不把庫侖摩擦視為固定黏性阻尼如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示造成偏離的合成觀察，以衰減包絡與頻率說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Damping ratio estimate, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Viscous damping and linear stiffness are known; Coulomb friction is not treated as constant viscous damping. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient. Explain which evidence in decay envelope and frequency distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「阻尼比估算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Damping ratio estimate\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足","本單元以衰減包絡與頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型自由衰減包絡、多振幅試驗及頻率估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve.","Use decay envelope and frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以衰減包絡與頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型自由衰減包絡、多振幅試驗及頻率估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use decay envelope and frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b346-v16-12","title":"阻尼比估算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Damping ratio estimate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「阻尼比估算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Damping ratio estimate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示。這個失效與「阻尼比估算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查衰減包絡與頻率，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient. This failure and a measurement bias in Damping ratio estimate can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check decay envelope and frequency rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用衰減包絡與頻率作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示。這個失效與「阻尼比估算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查衰減包絡與頻率，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient. This failure and a measurement bias in Damping ratio estimate can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check decay envelope and frequency rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「阻尼比估算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Damping ratio estimate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動"],"optionsEn":["Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b346-v16-13","title":"頻率比辨認：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Frequency-ratio identification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「頻率比辨認」如何影響浮動式道床減振的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Frequency-ratio identification” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floating-slab track vibration isolation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"激振與固有頻率的比值比任一頻率單獨更有判讀力。本模型把 f 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 8.59375 1。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。激振為單一頻率且固有頻率採同一工況。使用輸入頻譜與模態頻率作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「頻率比辨認」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The forcing-to-natural frequency ratio is more informative than either frequency alone. In this model, f is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 8.59375 1. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Excitation has one frequency and natural frequency uses the same operating condition. Use input spectrum and modal frequency as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Frequency-ratio identification” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：f=25 Hz, fn=3.2 Hz；y=f/fn=7.8125 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: f=25 Hz, fn=3.2 Hz; y=f/fn=7.8125 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「頻率比辨認」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Frequency-ratio identification”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-13-k1","title":"頻率比辨認","titleEn":"Frequency-ratio identification","text":"激振與固有頻率的比值比任一頻率單獨更有判讀力。本模型把 f 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 8.59375 1。","textEn":"The forcing-to-natural frequency ratio is more informative than either frequency alone. In this model, f is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「頻率比辨認」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Frequency-ratio identification\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動","激振與固有頻率的比值比任一頻率單獨更有判讀力。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance.","The forcing-to-natural frequency ratio is more informative than either frequency alone.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission."],"answer":1,"explanation":"激振與固有頻率的比值比任一頻率單獨更有判讀力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The forcing-to-natural frequency ratio is more informative than either frequency alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b346-v16-14","title":"頻率比辨認：定量估算","titleEn":"Frequency-ratio identification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「頻率比辨認」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Frequency-ratio identification” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：f=25 Hz, fn=3.2 Hz；y=f/fn=7.8125 1。只把 f 增加百分之十，y=8.59375 1。模型邊界：激振為單一頻率且固有頻率採同一工況；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: f=25 Hz, fn=3.2 Hz; y=f/fn=7.8125 1. Increasing only f with a ten-percent increase gives y=8.59375 1. Boundary: Excitation has one frequency and natural frequency uses the same operating condition; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以輸入頻譜與模態頻率區分模型與觀察，先用合成輸入力頻譜、模態試驗與相同載重紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use input spectrum and modal frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：f=25 Hz, fn=3.2 Hz；y=f/fn=7.8125 1。只把 f 增加百分之十，y=8.59375 1。模型邊界：激振為單一頻率且固有頻率採同一工況；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: f=25 Hz, fn=3.2 Hz; y=f/fn=7.8125 1. Increasing only f with a ten-percent increase gives y=8.59375 1. Boundary: Excitation has one frequency and natural frequency uses the same operating condition; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「頻率比辨認」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Frequency-ratio identification\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：f=25 Hz, fn=3.2 Hz；y=f/fn=7.8125 1。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Standing water can create additional contact damping.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: f=25 Hz, fn=3.2 Hz; y=f/fn=7.8125 1."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：f=25 Hz, fn=3.2 Hz；y=f/fn=7.8125 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: f=25 Hz, fn=3.2 Hz; y=f/fn=7.8125 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b346-v16-15","title":"頻率比辨認：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Frequency-ratio identification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「頻率比辨認」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Frequency-ratio identification” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以輸入頻譜與模態頻率區分模型與觀察，先用合成輸入力頻譜、模態試驗與相同載重紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「頻率比辨認」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use input spectrum and modal frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic input-force spectrum, modal test and matched loading records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Frequency-ratio identification. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「頻率比辨認」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出激振為單一頻率且固有頻率採同一工況如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動造成偏離的合成觀察，以輸入頻譜與模態頻率說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Frequency-ratio identification, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Excitation has one frequency and natural frequency uses the same operating condition. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance. Explain which evidence in input spectrum and modal frequency distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以輸入頻譜與模態頻率區分模型與觀察，先用合成輸入力頻譜、模態試驗與相同載重紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「頻率比辨認」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use input spectrum and modal frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic input-force spectrum, modal test and matched loading records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Frequency-ratio identification. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「頻率比辨認」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出激振為單一頻率且固有頻率採同一工況如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動造成偏離的合成觀察，以輸入頻譜與模態頻率說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Frequency-ratio identification, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Excitation has one frequency and natural frequency uses the same operating condition. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance. Explain which evidence in input spectrum and modal frequency distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「頻率比辨認」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Frequency-ratio identification\"?","options":["本單元以輸入頻譜與模態頻率區分模型與觀察，先用合成輸入力頻譜、模態試驗與相同載重紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承硬化會提高固有頻率"],"optionsEn":["Use input spectrum and modal frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support hardening raises natural frequency."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以輸入頻譜與模態頻率區分模型與觀察，先用合成輸入力頻譜、模態試驗與相同載重紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use input spectrum and modal frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b346-v16-16","title":"頻率比辨認：失效診斷","titleEn":"Frequency-ratio identification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「頻率比辨認」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Frequency-ratio identification” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動。這個失效與「頻率比辨認」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查輸入頻譜與模態頻率，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance. This failure and a measurement bias in Frequency-ratio identification can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check input spectrum and modal frequency rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用輸入頻譜與模態頻率作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動。這個失效與「頻率比辨認」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查輸入頻譜與模態頻率，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance. This failure and a measurement bias in Frequency-ratio identification can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check input spectrum and modal frequency rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「頻率比辨認」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Frequency-ratio identification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b346-v16-s3","title":"力傳遞率估算與支承數量分力","titleEn":"Force transmissibility estimate & Load per isolator","description":"本階段聚焦「力傳遞率估算」與「支承數量分力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Force transmissibility estimate\" and \"Load per isolator\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b346-v16-17","title":"力傳遞率估算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Force transmissibility estimate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「力傳遞率估算」如何影響浮動式道床減振的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Force transmissibility estimate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floating-slab track vibration isolation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"線性力傳遞率含共振分母與阻尼路徑。本模型把 r 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出減少為 0.12088 1。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。諧波力作用在質塊、基礎固定且線性穩態；不是任意基礎激振公式。使用輸入力與基礎反力作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「力傳遞率估算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Linear force transmissibility contains a resonance denominator and damping path. In this model, r is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output decreases to 0.12088 1. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Harmonic force acts on the mass with a fixed base in linear steady state; not a formula for arbitrary base excitation. Use input force and foundation reaction as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Force transmissibility estimate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：r=3 1, zeta=0.1 1；y=sqrt(1+(2*zeta*r)**2)/sqrt((1-r**2)**2+(2*zeta*r)**2)=0.145366 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: r=3 1, zeta=0.1 1; y=sqrt(1+(2*zeta*r)**2)/sqrt((1-r**2)**2+(2*zeta*r)**2)=0.145366 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「力傳遞率估算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Force transmissibility estimate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-17-k1","title":"力傳遞率估算","titleEn":"Force transmissibility estimate","text":"線性力傳遞率含共振分母與阻尼路徑。本模型把 r 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出減少為 0.12088 1。","textEn":"Linear force transmissibility contains a resonance denominator and damping path. In this model, r is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「力傳遞率估算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Force transmissibility estimate\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重心偏移使單支承過載","線性力傳遞率含共振分母與阻尼路徑。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports.","Linear force transmissibility contains a resonance denominator and damping path."],"answer":2,"explanation":"線性力傳遞率含共振分母與阻尼路徑。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Linear force transmissibility contains a resonance denominator and damping path. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b346-v16-18","title":"力傳遞率估算：定量估算","titleEn":"Force transmissibility estimate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「力傳遞率估算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Force transmissibility estimate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：r=3 1, zeta=0.1 1；y=sqrt(1+(2*zeta*r)**2)/sqrt((1-r**2)**2+(2*zeta*r)**2)=0.145366 1。只把 r 增加百分之十，y=0.12088 1。模型邊界：諧波力作用在質塊、基礎固定且線性穩態；不是任意基礎激振公式；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: r=3 1, zeta=0.1 1; y=sqrt(1+(2*zeta*r)**2)/sqrt((1-r**2)**2+(2*zeta*r)**2)=0.145366 1. Increasing only r with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.12088 1. Boundary: Harmonic force acts on the mass with a fixed base in linear steady state; not a formula for arbitrary base excitation; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以輸入力與基礎反力區分模型與觀察，先用模型輸入力與基礎反力的同步幅值及相位建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use input force and foundation reaction to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：r=3 1, zeta=0.1 1；y=sqrt(1+(2*zeta*r)**2)/sqrt((1-r**2)**2+(2*zeta*r)**2)=0.145366 1。只把 r 增加百分之十，y=0.12088 1。模型邊界：諧波力作用在質塊、基礎固定且線性穩態；不是任意基礎激振公式；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: r=3 1, zeta=0.1 1; y=sqrt(1+(2*zeta*r)**2)/sqrt((1-r**2)**2+(2*zeta*r)**2)=0.145366 1. Increasing only r with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.12088 1. Boundary: Harmonic force acts on the mass with a fixed base in linear steady state; not a formula for arbitrary base excitation; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「力傳遞率估算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Force transmissibility estimate\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：r=3 1, zeta=0.1 1。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：異物橋接會旁路隔振支承","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: r=3 1, zeta=0.1 1; y=sqrt(1+(2*zeta*r)**2)/sqrt((1-r**2)**2+(2*zeta*r)**2)=0.145366 1.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：r=3 1, zeta=0.1 1；y=sqrt(1+(2*zeta*r)**2)/sqrt((1-r**2)**2+(2*zeta*r)**2)=0.145366 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: r=3 1, zeta=0.1 1; y=sqrt(1+(2*zeta*r)**2)/sqrt((1-r**2)**2+(2*zeta*r)**2)=0.145366 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b346-v16-19","title":"力傳遞率估算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Force transmissibility estimate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「力傳遞率估算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Force transmissibility estimate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以輸入力與基礎反力區分模型與觀察，先用模型輸入力與基礎反力的同步幅值及相位建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「力傳遞率估算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use input force and foundation reaction to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synchronized model input-force and base-reaction amplitudes and phases, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Force transmissibility estimate. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「力傳遞率估算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出諧波力作用在質塊、基礎固定且線性穩態；不是任意基礎激振公式如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞造成偏離的合成觀察，以輸入力與基礎反力說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Force transmissibility estimate, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Harmonic force acts on the mass with a fixed base in linear steady state; not a formula for arbitrary base excitation. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission. Explain which evidence in input force and foundation reaction distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以輸入力與基礎反力區分模型與觀察，先用模型輸入力與基礎反力的同步幅值及相位建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「力傳遞率估算」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use input force and foundation reaction to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synchronized model input-force and base-reaction amplitudes and phases, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Force transmissibility estimate. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「力傳遞率估算」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出諧波力作用在質塊、基礎固定且線性穩態；不是任意基礎激振公式如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞造成偏離的合成觀察，以輸入力與基礎反力說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Force transmissibility estimate, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Harmonic force acts on the mass with a fixed base in linear steady state; not a formula for arbitrary base excitation. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission. Explain which evidence in input force and foundation reaction distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「力傳遞率估算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Force transmissibility estimate\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以輸入力與基礎反力區分模型與觀察，先用模型輸入力與基礎反力的同步幅值及相位建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承到底會使線性隔振失效"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use input force and foundation reaction to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以輸入力與基礎反力區分模型與觀察，先用模型輸入力與基礎反力的同步幅值及相位建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use input force and foundation reaction to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b346-v16-20","title":"力傳遞率估算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Force transmissibility estimate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「力傳遞率估算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Force transmissibility estimate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞。這個失效與「力傳遞率估算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查輸入力與基礎反力，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission. This failure and a measurement bias in Force transmissibility estimate can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check input force and foundation reaction rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用輸入力與基礎反力作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞。這個失效與「力傳遞率估算」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查輸入力與基礎反力，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission. This failure and a measurement bias in Force transmissibility estimate can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check input force and foundation reaction rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「力傳遞率估算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Force transmissibility estimate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重心偏移使單支承過載","過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports.","Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission."],"answer":2,"explanation":"過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b346-v16-21","title":"支承數量分力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Load per isolator: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「支承數量分力」如何影響浮動式道床減振的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Load per isolator” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floating-slab track vibration isolation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"均勻分力只適用對稱幾何與重心位置。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 13.4887 kN。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。支承對稱、剛度相同且重心居中；只算靜載。使用各支承壓縮與反力作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；重心偏移使單支承過載，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支承數量分力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Equal support load requires symmetric geometry and centre of mass. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 13.4887 kN. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Supports are symmetric, equally stiff and centered beneath the mass; static load only. Use compression and reaction at each support as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Load per isolator” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, n=8 count；y=m*g/n/1000=12.2625 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, n=8 count; y=m*g/n/1000=12.2625 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重心偏移使單支承過載」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支承數量分力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Load per isolator”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-21-k1","title":"支承數量分力","titleEn":"Load per isolator","text":"均勻分力只適用對稱幾何與重心位置。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 13.4887 kN。","textEn":"Equal support load requires symmetric geometry and centre of mass. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重心偏移使單支承過載 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支承數量分力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Load per isolator\" is correct?","options":["均勻分力只適用對稱幾何與重心位置。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重心偏移使單支承過載","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載"],"optionsEn":["Equal support load requires symmetric geometry and centre of mass.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload."],"answer":0,"explanation":"均勻分力只適用對稱幾何與重心位置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Equal support load requires symmetric geometry and centre of mass. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b346-v16-22","title":"支承數量分力：定量估算","titleEn":"Load per isolator: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支承數量分力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Load per isolator” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, n=8 count；y=m*g/n/1000=12.2625 kN。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=13.4887 kN。模型邊界：支承對稱、剛度相同且重心居中；只算靜載；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, n=8 count; y=m*g/n/1000=12.2625 kN. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=13.4887 kN. Boundary: Supports are symmetric, equally stiff and centered beneath the mass; static load only; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以各支承壓縮與反力區分模型與觀察，先用各支承模型力計、壓縮量及重心位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use compression and reaction at each support to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, n=8 count；y=m*g/n/1000=12.2625 kN。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=13.4887 kN。模型邊界：支承對稱、剛度相同且重心居中；只算靜載；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, n=8 count; y=m*g/n/1000=12.2625 kN. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=13.4887 kN. Boundary: Supports are symmetric, equally stiff and centered beneath the mass; static load only; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支承數量分力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Load per isolator\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, n=8 count；y=m*g/n/1000=12.2625 kN。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承硬化會提高固有頻率"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Standing water can create additional contact damping.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, n=8 count; y=m*g/n/1000=12.2625 kN.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support hardening raises natural frequency."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, n=8 count；y=m*g/n/1000=12.2625 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=10000 kg, g=9.81 m/s2, n=8 count; y=m*g/n/1000=12.2625 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b346-v16-23","title":"支承數量分力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Load per isolator: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支承數量分力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Load per isolator” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以各支承壓縮與反力區分模型與觀察，先用各支承模型力計、壓縮量及重心位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「支承數量分力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use compression and reaction at each support to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using individual model support force gauges, compression and center-of-mass location, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Load per isolator. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「支承數量分力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出支承對稱、剛度相同且重心居中；只算靜載如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由重心偏移使單支承過載造成偏離的合成觀察，以各支承壓縮與反力說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Load per isolator, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Supports are symmetric, equally stiff and centered beneath the mass; static load only. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports. Explain which evidence in compression and reaction at each support distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：重心偏移使單支承過載。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以各支承壓縮與反力區分模型與觀察，先用各支承模型力計、壓縮量及重心位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「支承數量分力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use compression and reaction at each support to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using individual model support force gauges, compression and center-of-mass location, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Load per isolator. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「支承數量分力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出支承對稱、剛度相同且重心居中；只算靜載如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由重心偏移使單支承過載造成偏離的合成觀察，以各支承壓縮與反力說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Load per isolator, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Supports are symmetric, equally stiff and centered beneath the mass; static load only. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports. Explain which evidence in compression and reaction at each support distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支承數量分力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Load per isolator\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示","本單元以各支承壓縮與反力區分模型與觀察，先用各支承模型力計、壓縮量及重心位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient.","Use compression and reaction at each support to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以各支承壓縮與反力區分模型與觀察，先用各支承模型力計、壓縮量及重心位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use compression and reaction at each support to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b346-v16-24","title":"支承數量分力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Load per isolator: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支承數量分力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Load per isolator” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"重心偏移使單支承過載。這個失效與「支承數量分力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查各支承壓縮與反力，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports. This failure and a measurement bias in Load per isolator can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check compression and reaction at each support rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用各支承壓縮與反力作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；重心偏移使單支承過載，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重心偏移使單支承過載」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"重心偏移使單支承過載。這個失效與「支承數量分力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查各支承壓縮與反力，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports. This failure and a measurement bias in Load per isolator can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check compression and reaction at each support rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支承數量分力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Load per isolator\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["重心偏移使單支承過載。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載"],"optionsEn":["A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload."],"answer":0,"explanation":"重心偏移使單支承過載。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b346-v16-s4","title":"剛度不均分力與間隙餘量檢查","titleEn":"Unequal-stiffness force share & Clearance reserve","description":"本階段聚焦「剛度不均分力」與「間隙餘量檢查」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Unequal-stiffness force share\" and \"Clearance reserve\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b346-v16-25","title":"剛度不均分力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Unequal-stiffness force share: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「剛度不均分力」如何影響浮動式道床減振的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Unequal-stiffness force share” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floating-slab track vibration isolation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"同位移支承中較硬者承受較大力。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 66 kN。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。剛性板保持兩支承同位移且無轉動；兩者皆接觸。使用支承高度與剛度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剛度不均分力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The stiffer support carries more force when displacement is shared. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 66 kN. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. A rigid plate maintains identical support displacement without rotation; both supports remain in contact. Use support height and stiffness as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Unequal-stiffness force share” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 kN, k1=30 kN/mm, k2=20 kN/mm；y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=60 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 kN, k1=30 kN/mm, k2=20 kN/mm; y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=60 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剛度不均分力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Unequal-stiffness force share”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-25-k1","title":"剛度不均分力","titleEn":"Unequal-stiffness force share","text":"同位移支承中較硬者承受較大力。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 66 kN。","textEn":"The stiffer support carries more force when displacement is shared. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「剛度不均分力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Unequal-stiffness force share\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載","同位移支承中較硬者承受較大力。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：異物橋接會旁路隔振支承"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload.","The stiffer support carries more force when displacement is shared.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同位移支承中較硬者承受較大力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The stiffer support carries more force when displacement is shared. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b346-v16-26","title":"剛度不均分力：定量估算","titleEn":"Unequal-stiffness force share: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剛度不均分力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Unequal-stiffness force share” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 kN, k1=30 kN/mm, k2=20 kN/mm；y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=60 kN。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=66 kN。模型邊界：剛性板保持兩支承同位移且無轉動；兩者皆接觸；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 kN, k1=30 kN/mm, k2=20 kN/mm; y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=60 kN. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=66 kN. Boundary: A rigid plate maintains identical support displacement without rotation; both supports remain in contact; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以支承高度與剛度區分模型與觀察，先用兩支承分力、共同位移及板體轉角建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use support height and stiffness to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 kN, k1=30 kN/mm, k2=20 kN/mm；y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=60 kN。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=66 kN。模型邊界：剛性板保持兩支承同位移且無轉動；兩者皆接觸；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 kN, k1=30 kN/mm, k2=20 kN/mm; y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=60 kN. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=66 kN. Boundary: A rigid plate maintains identical support displacement without rotation; both supports remain in contact; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「剛度不均分力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Unequal-stiffness force share\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承到底會使線性隔振失效","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 kN, k1=30 kN/mm, k2=20 kN/mm；y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=60 kN。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 kN, k1=30 kN/mm, k2=20 kN/mm; y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=60 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 kN, k1=30 kN/mm, k2=20 kN/mm；y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=60 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 kN, k1=30 kN/mm, k2=20 kN/mm; y=F*k1/(k1+k2)=60 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b346-v16-27","title":"剛度不均分力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Unequal-stiffness force share: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剛度不均分力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Unequal-stiffness force share” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以支承高度與剛度區分模型與觀察，先用兩支承分力、共同位移及板體轉角建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「剛度不均分力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use support height and stiffness to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using separate support forces, shared displacement and plate rotation, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Unequal-stiffness force share. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「剛度不均分力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出剛性板保持兩支承同位移且無轉動；兩者皆接觸如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載造成偏離的合成觀察，以支承高度與剛度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Unequal-stiffness force share, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: A rigid plate maintains identical support displacement without rotation; both supports remain in contact. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload. Explain which evidence in support height and stiffness distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以支承高度與剛度區分模型與觀察，先用兩支承分力、共同位移及板體轉角建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「剛度不均分力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use support height and stiffness to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using separate support forces, shared displacement and plate rotation, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Unequal-stiffness force share. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「剛度不均分力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出剛性板保持兩支承同位移且無轉動；兩者皆接觸如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載造成偏離的合成觀察，以支承高度與剛度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Unequal-stiffness force share, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: A rigid plate maintains identical support displacement without rotation; both supports remain in contact. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload. Explain which evidence in support height and stiffness distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「剛度不均分力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Unequal-stiffness force share\"?","options":["本單元以支承高度與剛度區分模型與觀察，先用兩支承分力、共同位移及板體轉角建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動"],"optionsEn":["Use support height and stiffness to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以支承高度與剛度區分模型與觀察，先用兩支承分力、共同位移及板體轉角建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use support height and stiffness to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b346-v16-28","title":"剛度不均分力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Unequal-stiffness force share: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剛度不均分力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Unequal-stiffness force share” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載。這個失效與「剛度不均分力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查支承高度與剛度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload. This failure and a measurement bias in Unequal-stiffness force share can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check support height and stiffness rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用支承高度與剛度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載。這個失效與「剛度不均分力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查支承高度與剛度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload. This failure and a measurement bias in Unequal-stiffness force share can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check support height and stiffness rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「剛度不均分力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Unequal-stiffness force share\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：異物橋接會旁路隔振支承"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b346-v16-29","title":"間隙餘量檢查：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Clearance reserve: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「間隙餘量檢查」如何影響浮動式道床減振的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Clearance reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floating-slab track vibration isolation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"靜壓縮與動態振幅都消耗同一間隙。本模型把 gap 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 14 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。動態量是朝限位方向的峰值位移；與靜壓縮共用同一基準。使用最小間隙與峰值位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；異物橋接會旁路隔振支承，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「間隙餘量檢查」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Static compression and dynamic amplitude consume the same clearance. In this model, gap is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 14 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Dynamic motion is peak displacement toward the stop and shares a datum with static compression. Use minimum clearance and peak displacement as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Clearance reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：gap=40 mm, static=24 mm, dynamic=6 mm；y=gap-static-dynamic=10 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: gap=40 mm, static=24 mm, dynamic=6 mm; y=gap-static-dynamic=10 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：異物橋接會旁路隔振支承」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「間隙餘量檢查」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Clearance reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-29-k1","title":"間隙餘量檢查","titleEn":"Clearance reserve","text":"靜壓縮與動態振幅都消耗同一間隙。本模型把 gap 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 14 mm。","textEn":"Static compression and dynamic amplitude consume the same clearance. In this model, gap is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：異物橋接會旁路隔振支承 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「間隙餘量檢查」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Clearance reserve\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：異物橋接會旁路隔振支承","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼","靜壓縮與動態振幅都消耗同一間隙。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Standing water can create additional contact damping.","Static compression and dynamic amplitude consume the same clearance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"靜壓縮與動態振幅都消耗同一間隙。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Static compression and dynamic amplitude consume the same clearance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b346-v16-30","title":"間隙餘量檢查：定量估算","titleEn":"Clearance reserve: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「間隙餘量檢查」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Clearance reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：gap=40 mm, static=24 mm, dynamic=6 mm；y=gap-static-dynamic=10 mm。只把 gap 增加百分之十，y=14 mm。模型邊界：動態量是朝限位方向的峰值位移；與靜壓縮共用同一基準；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: gap=40 mm, static=24 mm, dynamic=6 mm; y=gap-static-dynamic=10 mm. Increasing only gap with a ten-percent increase gives y=14 mm. Boundary: Dynamic motion is peak displacement toward the stop and shares a datum with static compression; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以最小間隙與峰值位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型最小淨距、靜壓縮及同步動態峰值建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use minimum clearance and peak displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：gap=40 mm, static=24 mm, dynamic=6 mm；y=gap-static-dynamic=10 mm。只把 gap 增加百分之十，y=14 mm。模型邊界：動態量是朝限位方向的峰值位移；與靜壓縮共用同一基準；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: gap=40 mm, static=24 mm, dynamic=6 mm; y=gap-static-dynamic=10 mm. Increasing only gap with a ten-percent increase gives y=14 mm. Boundary: Dynamic motion is peak displacement toward the stop and shares a datum with static compression; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「間隙餘量檢查」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Clearance reserve\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：gap=40 mm, static=24 mm, dynamic=6 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承硬化會提高固有頻率","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: gap=40 mm, static=24 mm, dynamic=6 mm; y=gap-static-dynamic=10 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support hardening raises natural frequency.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：gap=40 mm, static=24 mm, dynamic=6 mm；y=gap-static-dynamic=10 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: gap=40 mm, static=24 mm, dynamic=6 mm; y=gap-static-dynamic=10 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b346-v16-31","title":"間隙餘量檢查：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Clearance reserve: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「間隙餘量檢查」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Clearance reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以最小間隙與峰值位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型最小淨距、靜壓縮及同步動態峰值建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「間隙餘量檢查」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use minimum clearance and peak displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model minimum clearance, static compression and synchronous dynamic peaks, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Clearance reserve. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「間隙餘量檢查」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出動態量是朝限位方向的峰值位移；與靜壓縮共用同一基準如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由異物橋接會旁路隔振支承造成偏離的合成觀察，以最小間隙與峰值位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Clearance reserve, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Dynamic motion is peak displacement toward the stop and shares a datum with static compression. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support. Explain which evidence in minimum clearance and peak displacement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：異物橋接會旁路隔振支承。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以最小間隙與峰值位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型最小淨距、靜壓縮及同步動態峰值建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「間隙餘量檢查」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use minimum clearance and peak displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model minimum clearance, static compression and synchronous dynamic peaks, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Clearance reserve. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「間隙餘量檢查」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出動態量是朝限位方向的峰值位移；與靜壓縮共用同一基準如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由異物橋接會旁路隔振支承造成偏離的合成觀察，以最小間隙與峰值位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Clearance reserve, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Dynamic motion is peak displacement toward the stop and shares a datum with static compression. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support. Explain which evidence in minimum clearance and peak displacement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「間隙餘量檢查」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Clearance reserve\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以最小間隙與峰值位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型最小淨距、靜壓縮及同步動態峰值建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use minimum clearance and peak displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以最小間隙與峰值位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型最小淨距、靜壓縮及同步動態峰值建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use minimum clearance and peak displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b346-v16-32","title":"間隙餘量檢查：失效診斷","titleEn":"Clearance reserve: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「間隙餘量檢查」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Clearance reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"異物橋接會旁路隔振支承。這個失效與「間隙餘量檢查」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查最小間隙與峰值位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support. This failure and a measurement bias in Clearance reserve can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check minimum clearance and peak displacement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用最小間隙與峰值位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；異物橋接會旁路隔振支承，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：異物橋接會旁路隔振支承」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"異物橋接會旁路隔振支承。這個失效與「間隙餘量檢查」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查最小間隙與峰值位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support. This failure and a measurement bias in Clearance reserve can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check minimum clearance and peak displacement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「間隙餘量檢查」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Clearance reserve\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼","異物橋接會旁路隔振支承。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Standing water can create additional contact damping.","Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support."],"answer":2,"explanation":"異物橋接會旁路隔振支承。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Foreign material can bridge and bypass the isolation support. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b346-v16-s5","title":"積水附加質量與頻率降低敏感度","titleEn":"Water added mass & Frequency reduction sensitivity","description":"本階段聚焦「積水附加質量」與「頻率降低敏感度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Water added mass\" and \"Frequency reduction sensitivity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b346-v16-33","title":"積水附加質量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Water added mass: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「積水附加質量」如何影響浮動式道床減振的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Water added mass” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floating-slab track vibration isolation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"排水不良會增加質量且改變固有頻率。本模型把 rho 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 660 kg。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。水深及面積均勻且水全隨板體運動；不含流動與晃動。使用水位與模態頻率作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「積水附加質量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Poor drainage adds mass and changes natural frequency. In this model, rho is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 660 kg. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Water depth and area are uniform and water moves fully with the slab; flow and sloshing are excluded. Use water depth and modal frequency as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Standing water can create additional contact damping; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Water added mass” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=1000 kg/m3, A=20 m2, h=0.03 m；y=rho*A*h=600 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=1000 kg/m3, A=20 m2, h=0.03 m; y=rho*A*h=600 kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Standing water can create additional contact damping.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「積水附加質量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Water added mass”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-33-k1","title":"積水附加質量","titleEn":"Water added mass","text":"排水不良會增加質量且改變固有頻率。本模型把 rho 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 660 kg。","textEn":"Poor drainage adds mass and changes natural frequency. In this model, rho is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Standing water can create additional contact damping. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「積水附加質量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Water added mass\" is correct?","options":["排水不良會增加質量且改變固有頻率。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足"],"optionsEn":["Poor drainage adds mass and changes natural frequency.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Standing water can create additional contact damping.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve."],"answer":0,"explanation":"排水不良會增加質量且改變固有頻率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Poor drainage adds mass and changes natural frequency. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b346-v16-34","title":"積水附加質量：定量估算","titleEn":"Water added mass: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「積水附加質量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Water added mass” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=1000 kg/m3, A=20 m2, h=0.03 m；y=rho*A*h=600 kg。只把 rho 增加百分之十，y=660 kg。模型邊界：水深及面積均勻且水全隨板體運動；不含流動與晃動；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=1000 kg/m3, A=20 m2, h=0.03 m; y=rho*A*h=600 kg. Increasing only rho with a ten-percent increase gives y=660 kg. Boundary: Water depth and area are uniform and water moves fully with the slab; flow and sloshing are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以水位與模態頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型積水深度網格、總水量及振動頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use water depth and modal frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=1000 kg/m3, A=20 m2, h=0.03 m；y=rho*A*h=600 kg。只把 rho 增加百分之十，y=660 kg。模型邊界：水深及面積均勻且水全隨板體運動；不含流動與晃動；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=1000 kg/m3, A=20 m2, h=0.03 m; y=rho*A*h=600 kg. Increasing only rho with a ten-percent increase gives y=660 kg. Boundary: Water depth and area are uniform and water moves fully with the slab; flow and sloshing are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「積水附加質量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Water added mass\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承到底會使線性隔振失效","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=1000 kg/m3, A=20 m2, h=0.03 m；y=rho*A*h=600 kg。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只看峰值幅度會漏掉共振移動"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Bottoming out invalidates linear isolation.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=1000 kg/m3, A=20 m2, h=0.03 m; y=rho*A*h=600 kg.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Amplitude alone can miss a shifted resonance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=1000 kg/m3, A=20 m2, h=0.03 m；y=rho*A*h=600 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=1000 kg/m3, A=20 m2, h=0.03 m; y=rho*A*h=600 kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b346-v16-35","title":"積水附加質量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Water added mass: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「積水附加質量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Water added mass” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以水位與模態頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型積水深度網格、總水量及振動頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「積水附加質量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use water depth and modal frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model water-depth grid, total water volume and vibration frequency, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Water added mass. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「積水附加質量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出水深及面積均勻且水全隨板體運動；不含流動與晃動如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼造成偏離的合成觀察，以水位與模態頻率說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Water added mass, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Water depth and area are uniform and water moves fully with the slab; flow and sloshing are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Standing water can create additional contact damping. Explain which evidence in water depth and modal frequency distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Standing water can create additional contact damping. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以水位與模態頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型積水深度網格、總水量及振動頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「積水附加質量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use water depth and modal frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model water-depth grid, total water volume and vibration frequency, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Water added mass. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「積水附加質量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出水深及面積均勻且水全隨板體運動；不含流動與晃動如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼造成偏離的合成觀察，以水位與模態頻率說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Water added mass, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Water depth and area are uniform and water moves fully with the slab; flow and sloshing are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Standing water can create additional contact damping. Explain which evidence in water depth and modal frequency distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「積水附加質量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Water added mass\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：重心偏移使單支承過載","本單元以水位與模態頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型積水深度網格、總水量及振動頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A shifted centre of mass overloads individual supports.","Use water depth and modal frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以水位與模態頻率區分模型與觀察，先用模型積水深度網格、總水量及振動頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use water depth and modal frequency to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b346-v16-36","title":"積水附加質量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Water added mass: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「積水附加質量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Water added mass” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼。這個失效與「積水附加質量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查水位與模態頻率，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Standing water can create additional contact damping. This failure and a measurement bias in Water added mass can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check water depth and modal frequency rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用水位與模態頻率作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Standing water can create additional contact damping; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Standing water can create additional contact damping.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼。這個失效與「積水附加質量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查水位與模態頻率，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Standing water can create additional contact damping. This failure and a measurement bias in Water added mass can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check water depth and modal frequency rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「積水附加質量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Water added mass\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足"],"optionsEn":["Standing water can create additional contact damping.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve."],"answer":0,"explanation":"積水也可能形成額外接觸阻尼。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Standing water can create additional contact damping. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b346-v16-37","title":"頻率降低敏感度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Frequency reduction sensitivity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「頻率降低敏感度」如何影響浮動式道床減振的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Frequency reduction sensitivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floating-slab track vibration isolation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"增加質量會降低頻率，但也增加靜態壓縮。本模型把 k 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 3.1831 Hz。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。附加質量剛接於原質塊且剛度不變；支承仍在線性行程內。使用載重前後頻率與高度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「頻率降低敏感度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Added mass lowers frequency while increasing static compression. In this model, k is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 3.1831 Hz. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Added mass is rigidly attached and stiffness unchanged; supports remain within linear travel. Use frequency and height before and after added load as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Frequency reduction sensitivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg, dm=1000 kg；y=sqrt(k/(m+dm))/(2*pi)=3.03497 Hz。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg, dm=1000 kg; y=sqrt(k/(m+dm))/(2*pi)=3.03497 Hz.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「頻率降低敏感度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Frequency reduction sensitivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-37-k1","title":"頻率降低敏感度","titleEn":"Frequency reduction sensitivity","text":"增加質量會降低頻率，但也增加靜態壓縮。本模型把 k 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 3.1831 Hz。","textEn":"Added mass lowers frequency while increasing static compression. In this model, k is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「頻率降低敏感度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Frequency reduction sensitivity\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足","增加質量會降低頻率，但也增加靜態壓縮。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承硬化會提高固有頻率"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve.","Added mass lowers frequency while increasing static compression.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support hardening raises natural frequency."],"answer":1,"explanation":"增加質量會降低頻率，但也增加靜態壓縮。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Added mass lowers frequency while increasing static compression. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b346-v16-38","title":"頻率降低敏感度：定量估算","titleEn":"Frequency reduction sensitivity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「頻率降低敏感度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Frequency reduction sensitivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg, dm=1000 kg；y=sqrt(k/(m+dm))/(2*pi)=3.03497 Hz。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=3.1831 Hz。模型邊界：附加質量剛接於原質塊且剛度不變；支承仍在線性行程內；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg, dm=1000 kg; y=sqrt(k/(m+dm))/(2*pi)=3.03497 Hz. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.1831 Hz. Boundary: Added mass is rigidly attached and stiffness unchanged; supports remain within linear travel; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以載重前後頻率與高度區分模型與觀察，先用模型加重前後質量、靜態高度與模態頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use frequency and height before and after added load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg, dm=1000 kg；y=sqrt(k/(m+dm))/(2*pi)=3.03497 Hz。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=3.1831 Hz。模型邊界：附加質量剛接於原質塊且剛度不變；支承仍在線性行程內；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg, dm=1000 kg; y=sqrt(k/(m+dm))/(2*pi)=3.03497 Hz. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=3.1831 Hz. Boundary: Added mass is rigidly attached and stiffness unchanged; supports remain within linear travel; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「頻率降低敏感度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Frequency reduction sensitivity\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦阻尼不一定可由固定黏性係數表示","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：過大阻尼在高頻可增加傳遞","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg, dm=1000 kg。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction damping need not match a fixed viscous coefficient.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Excess damping can increase high-frequency transmission.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg, dm=1000 kg; y=sqrt(k/(m+dm))/(2*pi)=3.03497 Hz."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg, dm=1000 kg；y=sqrt(k/(m+dm))/(2*pi)=3.03497 Hz。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=4000000 N/m, m=10000 kg, dm=1000 kg; y=sqrt(k/(m+dm))/(2*pi)=3.03497 Hz. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b346-v16-39","title":"頻率降低敏感度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Frequency reduction sensitivity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「頻率降低敏感度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Frequency reduction sensitivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以載重前後頻率與高度區分模型與觀察，先用模型加重前後質量、靜態高度與模態頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「頻率降低敏感度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use frequency and height before and after added load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model masses, static heights and modal frequencies before and after added load, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Frequency reduction sensitivity. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「頻率降低敏感度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出附加質量剛接於原質塊且剛度不變；支承仍在線性行程內如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足造成偏離的合成觀察，以載重前後頻率與高度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Frequency reduction sensitivity, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Added mass is rigidly attached and stiffness unchanged; supports remain within linear travel. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve. Explain which evidence in frequency and height before and after added load distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以載重前後頻率與高度區分模型與觀察，先用模型加重前後質量、靜態高度與模態頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「頻率降低敏感度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use frequency and height before and after added load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model masses, static heights and modal frequencies before and after added load, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Frequency reduction sensitivity. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「頻率降低敏感度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出附加質量剛接於原質塊且剛度不變；支承仍在線性行程內如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足造成偏離的合成觀察，以載重前後頻率與高度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Frequency reduction sensitivity, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Added mass is rigidly attached and stiffness unchanged; supports remain within linear travel. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve. Explain which evidence in frequency and height before and after added load distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「頻率降低敏感度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Frequency reduction sensitivity\"?","options":["本單元以載重前後頻率與高度區分模型與觀察，先用模型加重前後質量、靜態高度與模態頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只檢查總剛度會漏掉局部過載"],"optionsEn":["Use frequency and height before and after added load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Checking total stiffness alone misses local overload."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以載重前後頻率與高度區分模型與觀察，先用模型加重前後質量、靜態高度與模態頻率建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use frequency and height before and after added load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b346-v16-40","title":"頻率降低敏感度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Frequency reduction sensitivity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b346-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「頻率降低敏感度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Frequency reduction sensitivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足。這個失效與「頻率降低敏感度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查載重前後頻率與高度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve. This failure and a measurement bias in Frequency reduction sensitivity can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check frequency and height before and after added load rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用載重前後頻率與高度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b346-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足。這個失效與「頻率降低敏感度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查載重前後頻率與高度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve. This failure and a measurement bias in Frequency reduction sensitivity can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check frequency and height before and after added load rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b346-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「頻率降低敏感度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Frequency reduction sensitivity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承硬化會提高固有頻率"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Support hardening raises natural frequency."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只追求低頻會忽略剩餘行程不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Pursuing low frequency alone ignores insufficient travel reserve. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b346-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b346-en.svg"}};
